menu "Improv Serial"

config ENABLE_IMPROV_SERIAL
    bool "Enable Improv Serial provisioning"
    default y
    help
        Adds the Improv Serial protocol (https://www.improv-wifi.com/serial/)
        so first-time Wi-Fi provisioning can be done from the same tab as the
        web flasher: ESP Web Tools flashes the firmware, then prompts for
        SSID / password and pushes them over the same USB serial connection.

        When enabled and no Wi-Fi credentials are stored, Improv becomes the
        sole Serial RX consumer for that boot -- the HomeSpan console "press
        any key" trigger is suppressed to avoid a second reader. After a
        successful association the credentials are persisted via HomeSpan's
        public API and setup continues in-process (no reboot); Improv
        remains the sole Serial RX consumer for the rest of this boot.

        The existing captive-portal / config-AP flow is unchanged and remains
        the reprovisioning path once credentials are stored.

        Default y: this is the intended provisioning experience. Disable it
        only if the firmware is too tight on flash (this component adds a
        few kilobytes) or if the console must stay usable when the device is
        unprovisioned.

endmenu
